BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20261026T165800Z
UID:a11cb847b167f6db3762e7d7aba4@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular: The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, presente
 d by Citizens\, returns October 1 &#8211\; November 1 with an all-new trai
 l of clever carvings guaranteed to make you smile\, groan\, and laugh out 
 loud. This year’s theme celebrates the art of the pun\, with thousands o
 f hand-carved pumpkins bringing witty wordplay to life through pop culture
  references\, playful characters and pun-believable scenes. From clever on
 e-liners to delightfully cheesy dad jokes\, there’s something to make ev
 ery guest grin as they stroll The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, where over 5\,000 
 glowing jack-o’-lanterns illuminate the Zoo. Don’t miss New England’
 s “must-see” family-friendly event of the Halloween season at Roger Wi
 lliams Park Zoo. All tickets must be purchased online in advance. Tickets 
 are required and sold online only. No refunds or rescheduling. Buy Tickets
 \n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacu
 lar/92071/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue\, Providence\, RI 0
 2907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacular/9207
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coastal Cruisers Fall Foliage Tours (+ Cider & Donuts)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTSTAMP:20261026T165800Z
UID:6d1f100e0388a1db3baa480bef75@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Coastal Cruisers Fall Foliage Tours (+ Cider &amp\; Donuts) Ex
 perience Newport at its most beautiful on our 2-hour Fall Foliage Tour. Tr
 avel along historic Bellevue Avenue\, past iconic estates\, and through sc
 enic\, tree-lined backroads showcasing classic New England fall colors. Yo
 ur local guide will share Newport’s history while taking you beyond the 
 traditional tourist routes\, with scenic stops for photos along the way. T
 o complete the fall experience\, enjoy complimentary apple cider and fresh
  apple cider donuts while taking in the crisp autumn air and beautiful New
 port scenery. 🍎🍩 What's Included Apple Cider and Donuts Itinerary Hi
 storic Bellevue Avenue: Cruise past Newport’s famous Gilded Age mansions
  surrounded by beautiful fall colors. Newport’s Scenic Backroads: Leave 
 the traditional tourist route and explore quiet\, tree-lined roads\, histo
 ric stone walls\, and classic New England scenery. Newport Country Club &a
 mp\; Ocean Drive Area: Travel through some of Newport’s most picturesque
  areas\, with sweeping landscapes and seasonal foliage. Scenic Photo Stops
 : Stop at select locations along the way for photos and time to take in th
 e fall scenery. Return Through Historic Newport: Finish the experience wit
 h more Newport history and views as we make our way back. Highlights 🍂 
 Newport’s Best Fall Scenery: Experience colorful tree-lined roads\, hist
 oric stone walls\, and classic New England landscapes. 🏛️ Gilded Age 
 Newport: Travel along Bellevue Avenue and see Newport’s iconic mansions 
 surrounded by autumn colors. 🌳 Beyond the Traditional Tour Route: Explo
 re quieter backroads and scenic areas near Newport Country Club that many 
 visitors never see. 📸 Picture-Perfect Stops: Enjoy opportunities to ste
 p out\, take photos\, and experience Newport during its most colorful seas
 on.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-fal
 l-foliage-tours-(%2b-cider-%26-donuts)/112431/
LOCATION:Coastal Cruisers\, 478 Thames Street\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-fall-foliage-t
 ours-(%2b-cider-%26-donuts)/112431/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTSTAMP:20261026T165800Z
UID:aa134d2beb4420287fbab1db55a5@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blood Moon (With LED Lights) - Painting Class
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTSTAMP:20261026T165800Z
UID:13b93d9f8e2c328ec2773b63e4a7@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:🖌️ IN-STUDIO SESSION DETAILS Reserve your spot and enjoy 
 a complimentary beverage—choose from soda\, beer\, or wine (21+ with val
 id ID). Additional drinks will be available for purchase. Immerse yourself
  in a fun and creative atmosphere while painting your own unique masterpie
 ce! Recommended for ages 14 and up. ⏰ ARRIVAL TIME Our studio opens 30 m
 inutes prior to class time. We recommend arriving 15&#8211\;30 minutes ear
 ly to find parking\, grab a drink\, and get settled. Please note: If you a
 rrive late\, the artist may not be able to fill you in on the steps you mi
 ssed\, as they will be focused on guiding the rest of the class. If you ar
 rive more than 20 minutes late\, we kindly ask that you do not join the se
 ssion. Late arrivals can be disruptive and may not have enough time to com
 plete the painting. Unfortunately\, we cannot offer refunds or reschedules
  for late arrivals. 🚗 PARKING INFO Our studio is located at 150 Main St
 reet (rear entrance)\, Pawtucket\, Rhode Island\, and we have two FREE par
 king lots: 🚗 One directly attached to our entrance 🚗 A second lot ju
 st one building down on the same side of the street — clearly labeled 
 🪑 WANT TO SIT WITH FRIENDS? If you purchased 2 or more tickets in one t
 ransaction\, we’ll automatically seat your group together. If you booked
  separately but want to sit with someone\, please include their first and 
 last names in the “Additional Information / Order Notes” field during 
 checkout. 🔄 RESCHEDULING &amp\; CANCELLATION POLICY All reservations ar
 e non-refundable. However\, if you need to reschedule\, you may request a 
 reschedule voucher at least 48 hours before your session. You can do this 
 easily on our website — just [click here]. No-shows cannot be reschedule
 d. 🚨 CLASS CANCELLATION Classes may be canceled due to low attendance. 
 In this case\, we’ll notify you and issue a voucher for a future session
 . We appreciate your understanding and look forward to welcoming you to a 
 future class! ❄️ INCLEMENT WEATHER POLICY Because New England weather 
 can be unpredictable\, we typically wait until a few hours before class to
  make final decisions. If we cancel due to snow or other severe weather\, 
 we’ll email you a voucher for a future session. Have more questions? Che
 ck out our [Frequently Asked Questions] page — just [click here].\n\nSou
 rce: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/blood-moon-(with-led-lights)-p
 ainting-class/111663/
LOCATION:Paint & Vino\, 150 Main Street\, Pawtucket\, 02860
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/blood-moon-(with-led-lights)-pa
 inting-class/111663/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Bike Rides in 2026 🚲
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTSTAMP:20261026T165800Z
UID:fa1a26f564edb25279ff613a44d2@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Full Moon Rides: The Ocean Loop by Sunset and Moonrise Newport
  feels a lot different at night\, especially in the silver glow of a full 
 moon with the line of bike lights piercing the evening twilight and the dr
 umbeat of waves lapping on the rocky shore. Our monthly Full Moon Rides &#
 8211\; Sponsored by AARP Rhode Island have returned for the 2026 season. T
 hese scenic evening group rides wind along the Newport shoreline\, delight
 ing first-timers and returning riders alike. A Full Moon Ride is social an
 d easygoing\; the pace is patient\, nobody gets left behind\, and particip
 ants are welcome to finish their journey with food and libations. The Full
  Moon Ride coastal route will bring us past scenic harbor\, bay\, and ocea
 n views &#8211\; lit first by the setting sun\, and then by the rising moo
 n. We’ll ride 15 miles on Newport’s scenic roads and coastline\, aroun
 d the beautiful Ocean Loop\, and and back into town. These rides have limi
 ted capacity\, so be sure to register as each date’s tickets become avai
 lable. All of the 2026 dates are listed below! Suggested Donation: $10 per
  Rider. Donations are not a requirement. Donations of all sizes are welcom
 e\, and support Bike Newport’s inclusive programs for bike safety educat
 ion and advocacy. Thank you! We require all riders to kindly pre-register 
 on Eventbrite for our ride-planning purposes. Riders must be at least 18 y
 ears of age. Registration for subsequent dates becomes available as soon a
 s the preceding ride has ended. Please bookmark this page in your web brow
 ser to refer back for all the relevant registration links\, updates\, and 
 announcements. All the Details: 20-30 minutes before the start of each rid
 e we’ll gather at Equality Park on Broadway in downtown Newport\, as mar
 ked by the star on the map\, adjacent to Parlor Bar &amp\; Kitchen (at 200
  Broadway). The ride lasts roughly two hours from departure\, returning to
  our starting spot. Wednesday\, April 1: Pink Moon - gather 6:10pm\, start
  6:40\, sunset 7:10\, moonrise 7:03 Friday\, May 1: Flower Moon - gather 6
 :40pm\, start 7:10\, sunset 7:43\, moonrise at 8:07 Sunday\, May 31: Blue 
 Moon/Micro Full Moon - gather 7:30pm\, start 8:00\, sunset 8:12\, moonrise
  9:04 Monday\, June 29: Strawberry Moon/ Micro Full Moon - gather 7:10pm\,
  start 7:40\, sunset 8:23\, moonrise 8:40 Wednesday\, July 29: Buck Moon -
  gather 6:55pm\, start 7:25\, sunset 8:05\, moonrise 8:23 Thursday\, Augus
 t 27: Sturgeon Moon - gather 5:45pm\, start 6:15\, sunset 7:26\, moonrise 
 7:15 Saturday\, September 26: Corn Moon - gather 4:55pm\, start 5:25\, sun
 set 6:35\, moonrise 6:23 Monday\, October 26: Hunter's Moon - gather 4:15p
 m\, start 4:45\, sunset 5:47\, moonrise 5:45 You can access the route here
 . The route begins at Equality Park. Once we reach King’s Park\, our coa
 stal route will bring us past scenic harbor\, bay\, and ocean views &#8211
 \; lit first by the setting sun\, and then by the rising full moon. Requir
 ements: Important: You must be able to ride 15 miles comfortably at 10mph 
 with traffic and know how to use your gears for hills (there are several.)
 This is a NIGHT ride\, we will be riding on dark roads. A helmet\, bright 
 front headlight\, and rear red blinking light are required to participate.
  Ensure your bike is in good working order before arriving. Be sure your l
 ights are well charged. If riding an e-bike\, ensure it is charged and in 
 fully working condition Please also bring your high viz vest/jacket\, wate
 r bottle\, and bicycle lock. Check your air pressure\, brakes\, and gears 
 If you start on the ride and are then not able to continue on the ride\, y
 ou are responsible for getting yourself home. Suggested Donation: $10 per 
 Rider. Dress for the weather! We will cancel the ride if weather/road cond
 itions are not safe and attempt a reschedule within 3 days. Keep an eye on
  our social media @BikeNewportRI and check this web page for updates.\n\nS
 ource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/full-moon-bike-rides-in-2026
 -%f0%9f%9a%b2/109471/
LOCATION:Equality Park\, Equality Park W\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/full-moon-bike-rides-in-2026-%f
 0%9f%9a%b2/109471/
END:VEVENT
